{
  "content": "{\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"proved_partial_result\",\n      \"statement\": \"Fix an integer h>B and ρ>0. Let A={Δ≤B}. For each composition u=(u_1,…,u_n) in A, choose the least index m∈{0,…,n−1} attaining the maximum of s_j. Define the donor D(u)=u_{m+1} when m≥1, and D(u)=u_1 when m=0. If D(u)≥ρd+h, transfer h units across the edge adjacent to m: for m≥1, replace (u_m,u_{m+1}) by (u_m+h,u_{m+1}−h); for m=0, replace (u_n,u_1) by (u_n+h,u_1−h). The total remains K.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"injection\",\n      \"statement\": \"For m≥1 this operation raises only s_m by h; for m=0 it lowers every s_j, j≥1, by h while leaving s_0=0. Since the original chosen vertex was maximal and h>B, the image has a unique maximum and Δ>B. Its unique maximum identifies m, after which the transfer is reversible. Hence the map is injective from A∩{D≥ρd+h} into {Δ>B}.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"exact_weight_comparison\",\n      \"statement\": \"Writing w_d(v)=binom(v+d−1,d−1), increasing the recipient cannot decrease its weight. For donor v≥ρd+h, w_d(v−h)/w_d(v)=∏_{r=0}^{h−1}(v−r)/(v+d−1−r)≥(ρ/(ρ+1))^h. Therefore, with c_{ρ,h}=(ρ/(ρ+1))^h, exact weighted mass satisfies W(Δ>B)≥c_{ρ,h} W(A∩{D≥ρd+h}).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"conditional_conclusion\",\n      \"statement\": \"If one proves the finite inequality P(D≥ρd+h | Δ≤B)≥q for constants ρ,q>0 independent of R, then p=P(Δ>B) obeys p≥c_{ρ,h}q(1−p), hence p≥c_{ρ,h}q/(1+c_{ρ,h}q)>0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"scope_distinction\",\n      \"statement\": \"This is only an exact endpoint-conditioned composition-law reduction. It supplies no first-passage transfer and proves no Collatz-array claim.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"claim_status\": \"PARTIAL: a bounded-distortion injection reduces GAP-LOWER-BOUND to one explicit donor lower-tail inequality, but that inequality is not established from the supplied assumptions.\",\n  \"first_missing_step\": \"Prove that for the least maximizing vertex M of the exact weighted bridge, its adjacent donor satisfies P(D≥ρd+h | Δ≤B)≥q for some fixed ρ,q>0 uniformly as R=dn→∞ and d is a fixed positive constant times log R. A marginal block lower-tail estimate alone is insufficient because M is path-dependent; a union bound over n can fail for small logarithmic constants.\",\n  \"unexpected_findings\": []\n}",
